                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "86d42553-23dd-3244-9fff-78bd164b308c",
                        "entry_id": "91d4048f-f615-3e3c-966c-751d687af7fc",
                        "glosses": [
                            "sprzęt laboratoryjny lub urządzenie przemysłowe, służące do pochłaniania (absorpcji) niektórych składników mieszaniny gazowej przez ciecz"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a6cd5c3f-2fd8-4e5b-bf14-8fca2ba9a54b",
                                "sense_id": "86d42553-23dd-3244-9fff-78bd164b308c",
                                "text": "Gaz doprowadzany był do absorberów stojących wzdłuż ściany."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "788370a8-0b1b-4240-aaa2-351a9e249f9a",
                        "source_entry_id": "91d4048f-f615-3e3c-966c-751d687af7fc",
                        "source_sense_id": "86d42553-23dd-3244-9fff-78bd164b308c",
                        "target_lang_word": "absorber",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "absorber",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "20eabe03-4f4c-3139-85e3-c7508a435502",
                                        "entry_id": "99ce9df5-bca0-37be-9a71-e131b5865d0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that absorbs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32ff9b45-5f09-46ab-aece-aedda17dc78c",
                                                "sense_id": "20eabe03-4f4c-3139-85e3-c7508a435502",
                                                "text": "[…] these Symptoms are only curred, by such Medicines as correct the Acidity and Acrimony of the Blood, viz. When it most partakes of Acrimony by sweet diaphoretick Decoctions, or some sort of Acids, which dull and take off their corroding Edges, or when they are more Acid, by volatile Salts that carry them off by Sweat or Urine; or by Acid Absorbers, which by correcting the Acidities of the Pancreatick Juice, leave the Ferment of the Liver more predominant […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "165d0975-7aea-4fdd-8b55-0b502e0ad861",
                                                "sense_id": "20eabe03-4f4c-3139-85e3-c7508a435502",
                                                "text": "1756, Thomas Amory, The Life of John Buncle, Esq., London: J. Noon, Chapter 36 “Remarks on the delluge,” p. ,\nThe swallows especially must do great work in the case, if we take into their number not only very many open gulphs or chasms, the depth of which no line or sound can reach; but likewise the communications of very many parts of the sea, and of many great unfathomable lochs, with the abyss. These absorbers could easily receive what had before come out of them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4fb169d8-9550-4287-a443-ec20fd942af7",
                                                "sense_id": "20eabe03-4f4c-3139-85e3-c7508a435502",
                                                "text": "Which can be ignited the more easily with a burning-glass, black or white paper?\nBlack paper, since it is a much better absorber of heat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01e97102-26ae-3705-ac7c-7167a3439896",
                                        "entry_id": "99ce9df5-bca0-37be-9a71-e131b5865d0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that absorbs.",
                                            "A device which causes gas or vapor to be absorbed by a liquid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "481c61c4-1e45-32d8-a7a9-65ea9a0c1a5c",
                                        "entry_id": "99ce9df5-bca0-37be-9a71-e131b5865d0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something that absorbs.",
                                            "A material that absorbs neutrons in a reactor."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8932af4a-d306-30b9-a1c6-ad697ca51285",
                                        "entry_id": "99ce9df5-bca0-37be-9a71-e131b5865d0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who absorbs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09f29987-eb19-4bea-8233-31764016de57",
                                                "sense_id": "8932af4a-d306-30b9-a1c6-ad697ca51285",
                                                "text": "Old Lady Dacier’s bluntness in speaking of her grandson would have shocked Lady Wathin as much as it astonished, had she been less of an ardent absorber of aristocratic manners."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23fd18b0-d4d0-4ffd-96d7-8c1fa0682566",
                                                "sense_id": "8932af4a-d306-30b9-a1c6-ad697ca51285",
                                                "text": "[…] since few wanted mosaics any more he had turned to fresco, becoming the greatest absorber and eclectic in Italy. He had learned everything that the earlier fresco painters, from the time of Cimabue, had to teach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f7c1664-62d7-4d6b-8b3e-c1592f98e8f5",
                                                "sense_id": "8932af4a-d306-30b9-a1c6-ad697ca51285",
                                                "text": "[…] Walter D. (“Walt”) DeLasandro Jr. had been able to bill her parents $130 an hour plus expenses for being put in the middle and playing the role of mediator and absorber of shit from both sides while she (i.e., the depressed person, as a child) had had to perform essentially the same coprophagous services on a more or less daily basis for free […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5edd0a04-83c7-321c-a104-83f679cda63f",
                                        "entry_id": "99ce9df5-bca0-37be-9a71-e131b5865d0f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A set that, under suitable transformations, can contain any set from a given class within a topological space."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ff8816b6-df1a-4c7a-ac26-8ba9642d507d",
                                                "sense_id": "5edd0a04-83c7-321c-a104-83f679cda63f",
                                                "text": "By proposition 6.5.4, X is a skeletoid and hence an absorber by theorem 6.5.1."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "91858495-586e-433c-ba60-a6d141fda951",
                                                "sense_id": "5edd0a04-83c7-321c-a104-83f679cda63f",
                                                "text": "Skeletoids and absorbers play an important role in infinite-dimensional topology. The existence and uniqueness of skeletoids (and absorbers) with respect to certain collections allow one to study completely metrizable infinite-dimensional manifolds by using the technique of compact manifolds, incomplete manifolds by those of complete ones and so on."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
